in Peking, "I don''t mean the Peking committee," there are two independent kingdoms, "你们去猜"); [[w.dikotter-cultural-revolution]], 25 n.35 (two factions, a socialist and a capitalist; "In Beijing, and I don''t mean the Beijing party committee, there are two independent kingdoms"); [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 6 (December 1964, no day: two "independent kingdoms" in Peking, the Secretariat under Deng Xiaoping and the State Planning Commission under Li Fuchun); [[w.zhu-de-nianpu-xinbian]], III, 1925 (Dec. 27, 1964; Zhu De 朱德 attends the Central Work Conference 中央工作会议). Made public: 1996. Check: MacFarquhar (13) does not date the rescinding, nor name the directive. Check: the number of the directive of Dec. 31; the book has No. 814, the Wengao No. 815 (III, 425 n.142). Check: units F–G, the issue of Dec. 28 and the General Office''s notice of Dec. 31 (XVII, 485 n.1), are acts of other days. See [[cal.1964-12-15.china-leadership]]. To check: the document "Some Problems Now Raised in the Rural Socialist Education Movement" (Central Committee [64] 811, stopped Dec. 31, 1964; named by [[w.zedong-mao-zedong-nianpu]], V, Dec. 15, 1964); [[w.tse-tung-miscellany-of-mao-tse]], 2, 427 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 424 n.134a); [[w.jin-1949-1989-niande-zhongguo]], 603 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 424 n.134b); the seventeen articles, the work conference''s minutes of Dec. 27, 1964, in [[w.zedong-jianguo-yilai-mao-zedong]], 11, 280, 283–4 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 424 n.135b); [[w.yibo-ruogan-zhongda-juece-yu-1991-93]], 2, 1128 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 425 n.139); the Center''s directive No. 814 of Dec. 31, 1964, cancelling No. 811, in [[w.yibo-ruogan-zhongda-juece-yu-1991-93]], 2, 1131–2 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 425 n.142c); Central Committee, Zhongfa [64] 811, Dec. 28, 1964, issuing the minutes (seventeen points) (cited by [[w.jianguo-yilai-mao-zedong]], XVII, 485 n.1b); Central Committee General Office, notice of Dec. 31, 1964 stopping the issue of Zhongfa [64] 811, to be destroyed (cited by [[w.jianguo-yilai-mao-zedong]], XVII, 485 n.1c); [[w.xianzhi-mao-zedong-zhuan-1949]], 1373 (cited by [[w.dikotter-cultural-revolution]], 25 n.35); [[w.zhongguo-gongchandang-lishi-dashiji]], 269 (cited by [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 6 n.12). Names: Mao Zedong, Chen Boda, Zhu De, Dong Biwu, Lu Dingyi.'
