-    n: '[[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 24; [[w.jianguo-yilai-mao-zedong]], XVIII, 175–177 (Dec. 2, 1965; Mao''s note of Dec. 2 on Lin Biao''s forwarding of the Lanzhou Military Region Party committee''s report of Nov. 7 on the 55th Division''s emergency war preparation: fully agrees with Lin''s view; the division''s case probably like the others''; may it go to all military regions, services and arms down to division Party committees; those who do not believe in prominence for politics, who comply in form and spread eclecticism, that is opportunism, are to be watched; to go first to Liu Shaoqi, Zhou and Peng Zhen); [[w.peng-zhen-nianpu-1902]], IV, 451 (Dec. 2, 1965; Peng Zhen, with Liu Shaoqi and Zhou Enlai, receives Mao''s comment on the Lanzhou Military Region committee''s report on the 55th Division; Peng then forwards it, as Mao directs, to the military regions, services and arms and the army and division Party committees); [[w.jian-zhou-enlai]], 531 (Mao, on a report Lin had sent him, endorses "highlighting politics" and denounces "those who have spread eclecticism [that is, opportunism]" in the army; he has the words relayed to Zhou, Liu and the other leaders); [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 27 (Mao''s comment on Lin''s letter of Nov. 18 and the Lanzhou Military Region''s material, wholly agreeing). Made public: 2006. To check: Mao Zedong, "Fandui zhezhongzhuyide wenti" (On Opposing Eclecticism), in [[w.mao-zedong-sixiang-wan]], 149 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 24 n.45); Party committee of the Lanzhou Military Region, report on giving prominence to politics in the 55th Division''s emergency war preparation (ordered to the Sino-Indian border in mid- and late Sept. 1965, then a week of motorized and foot-march exercise), Nov. 7, 1965, sent to Mao by Lin Biao Nov. 18 (cited by [[w.jianguo-yilai-mao-zedong]], XVIII, 176 n.1); Lin Biao, letter to Mao Zedong of Dec. 3, 1965 accepting Mao''s note, to be sent to Liu Shaoqi, Zhou and P